Dunno about creating another account, but one way to grant access is to
install sudo. It can be used to grant a user full super-user access, or
limit them to only one particular privileged operation without having to
share the root password.

I think one of the cooler features of sudo is E-mail notification to
root when an unauthorized access is attempted... Also does a good job of
CYA for sysadmins since it keeps a rather detailed log of everything
done through sudo (some people install sudo and delete su).

The official web page for sudo seems to be dead at this moment. but you
can download it from:

