I haven't tried the TEAC CD-R55S personally but cdrecord works with
YAMAHA 400at recorders.  Do not use a wide scsi controller to talk
to the recorder though.  There are some interaction problems that
may occur.


Just get a copy of cdrecord-1.6.1 from

	ftp://ftp.fokus.gmd.de/pub/unix/cdrecord/cdrecord-1.6.1.tar.gz

You need to have gmake (gnumake) in your PATH.

Extract the tar file, cd into the extracted directory and type

Gmake -C lib CC=cc WARN=-w LD=cc
Gmake -C cdrecord CC=cc WARN=-w LD=cc
Gmake -C mkisofs-1.12b4 CC=cc WARN=-w LD=cc


Sean



