Thanks! I found out a little bit more gory details about this, for
anyone else who might be interested.

    The micro-code in the mcode chip on the 1742A is propritary and
Adaptec does not have the G.2 revision, you can only get it through
Digital. The "I" revision would work fine for Linux or NT but not
for Digital UNIX.  After digging in the news for a while I finally
came up with a part number 23-681E6-00 and ordered 3 of them since
they where only 3 bucks a piece. This EPROM is "suppose" to replace
the mcode prom at position U10 on the 1742A to convert the card to
an Alpha compatible card.

    Now I just need to get a compatible disk for the root filesystem and
    I should be up and running ::crosses fingers and knocks on wood::



