> On a V4.x system with C2 security setup if someone locks their account after
> incorrectly entering the password say 3 times we use XIsso or dxaccounts to
> unlock the account. When I do out of hours support with a laptop at home I
> can't use the GUIs because the I can't run an X server on the laptop. So I
> thought I could edit the /tcb/files/auth/a...z files manually. I thought that
> when an account gets locked the u_lock field in /tcb/files/auth/a...z is:
> u_lock
> and when it is not locked it is:
> u_lock@
> When I have looked at locked accounts this doesn't seem to be the case, they
> all show u_lock@ whether they are locked or not.
> Anybody know any different ?

When user locks his/her account through several bad login attempts, "u_lock@"
doesn't change. Instead, there is another field, "u_numunsuc#<NUM>". That field
counts how many times the bad login has been attempted. Delete that field and
you have unlocked the account.

Nix.
