> Tommy
> tfoley@eng.uab.edu

I would have thought that you could boot in single user mode, even with a
fulldisk. Once there, do
/sbin/bcheckrc
and root and usr should be mounted read-write, and you ought to be able to
delete the necessary files.

The mount command you need is something like

mount -t advfs usr_domain#usr /tmp/tom

but you then need a symbolic link from /etc/fdmns/usr_domain/rz16g  ->
/dev/rz16g.
I suggest you read about AdvFS in the manuals before going too far down this
road
though.

