I've seen similar problems in other freeware source code and have used
the following perl script to fix it.

#!/usr/local/bin/perl
$file = @ARGV[0];
$filetmp = "$file.xxx";
open(OUTFILE, ">$filetmp") || die "$0: can't open $filetmp\n";
select(OUTFILE);
#printf "%s\n", $file;
while (<>)
{
 $a = $_;
 if ($a =~ /#/) {
    $a =~ s/^ +//;
    $a =~ s/^\t+//;
 }
 print $a;
}
rename($filetmp,$file);

(perl isn't my strongest language so it's probably a pretty average script. 
Looking back at it, I'm not even sure how it works!)

You could then run it something like:

find . -exec fixdefines.pl {} \;

under the source code directory.

