Hi,

There is no tool or option in the DIGITAL UNIX Developers' Toolkit (or the
other UNIX programming tools offered by Compaq) that profiles real time,
at least not yet. You can manually insert calls to gettimeofday(), or you
can write your own atom tool to call it at every procedure call or return,
being careful not to instrument the system libraries and to write
thread-safe code.

Also note that multi-threaded programs are supported by the tools you mention 
only if those programs are linked with libpthread; that is, if they use
either the CMA or POSIX (pthread) interfaces to libpthread. Other 
implementations of pthreads are not supported by these tools.

	John P Williams

