> > > The idea behind "retiring user" still eludes me. A retired user cannot
> > 
> > I always presumed it was to prevent UID reuse.
> 
> For what purpose?

I think that the most common problem of UID reuse is inheriting access
to files through ACLs that contain that UID. The problem can be worked
around (in fact, I think it should be done this way) by only using
group entries in ACLs and religiously cleaning up groups when a UID is
decommissioned (the owner of the file is still a problem however),
but "better safe than sorry" is the modus operandi of many sys
admins. For them, retiring a user is obviously desirable.

