Anatoly Oreshkin wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> I am running Digital Unix v3.2 on Alpha Server/100.
> Disk space of anonymous ftp is about to be exhausted.
> Of course I might extend disk space just by moving entire anonymous
> ftp to  larger file system but I havn't such large file system.
> I have total enough space in several file systems. So I  would like
> anonymous ftp to occupy disk space in several file systems.
> Unfortunately symbolic links do not work.
> 
> May be to use AdvFS ?
> Any ideas ?

Anonymous FTP issues chroot to its home directory. That makes anything above
~ftp/ directory structure invisible. The only way to increase the space, aside
from moving to another file system, is to mount another file system somwhere
under ~ftp/.

I don't think this helps you.

Nix.



