Dagnmr Galama wrote:
> 
> Hi there,
> 
> What setting should I take a look at, when I can ping a system  but cannot
> telnet to it. It is telnetable, but only from systems that don't reach this
> system with ping.

??????

The only two legitimate ways to restrict PING are:

1. Fu## up the routing, so no IP packets from a certain point reach you
(or that node).
2. Implement IP Filter access (V4.0 only)

Both of these would restrict IP and, consequently, PING. Your case is a
weird one. If you can telnet to a machine, then IP is reaching it. It
must ping back, there's no way to divert that. Unless you have your own
TCP/IP implementation.

Perhaps you should give more info on the system in question.

Nix.



