in /etc/passwd what is definitively a TROUBLE, because some of older
applications that I run, test existence of user by finding his login
name in this file.

On the other hand, it probably is not good idea just to remove a line
from /etc/passwd. If it was, then why'd "userdel" in "removeuser"
started yelling:

Working ...userdel: Error: modification of a retired user is not
allowed.

