When you delete a user, you may want to verify that there are no files hanging
arouynd that is owned by that user.  You can do that with

  find / -user <usder_name>  -print


You may also want to check if that user is listed in the /etc/group file.

I do not have Enhanced Security, so I can't help on that.

Steen


