Hi,

well, several things.
1) install Open3d (and PAK)
2) shutdown
3) install the card in a pci slot
4) boot with the generic kernel
5) build a new configuration file with `sizer`,compare
it with your file and edit your existing file accordingly.
(pci slots, name of the graphics card, it should be pvp0 ...)
6) build a new kernel with doconfig and boot it
7) enjoy (hopefully)

I have the same card and I am not very happy with it.
There seems to be a bug in the driver because graphics
(OpenGL or not) are sometimes delayed, very strange problem.
I talked to product manager of Open3D and he promised to
help me but nothing happened. I tried to remind him two times
but he doesn't reply any more.

Good luck with your card
Christian



