>
> I am getting some "unresolvable" messages while running an executable under
> 4.0B, CXX 6.1-027.  I find there is now a new libcxx.so, under
> /usr/ccs/lib/cmplrs/cxx that contains the text for this unresolvable symbol.
> Presumably, cxx is linking against the older libcxx.so in /usr/shlib.  I just
> recently upgraded cxx from 5.4 to 6.1.  Did I omit a step in the cxx
> installation process?
>

The history behind this is that the V6.0 (and above) C++ compiler required
new runtime support to implement the ANSI/ISO C++ Standard.  On 4.0D
and above systems, the libcxx.so that goes with the base OS, has the 
support.

To support prior versions of the OS, libcxx.so was shipped with the 
compiler kit and the compiler added the -rpath and -L to look at
libcxx.so in the /usr/lib/cmplrs/cxx area.


An updated libcxx.so has been placed into the UNIX patch kit stream and 
should be downloadable from:

http://www1.service.digital.com/patches/

Click on Search Engine, then search for libcxx.so - you'll find patches 
and descriptions of use of the cxx compiler to use the installed libcxx.so
instead of the one in the /usr/lib/cmplers/cxx area.


