Pui Ming WONG wrote:
> 
> Under DG unix 3.2c (version we are running), i see many files under
> /tcb/files/auth/a /tcb/files/auth/b ... /tcb/files/auth/z  ... etc
> with the same name as user-accounts.

This a shadow password database + other C2 security info on each user on the
system.

> Their dates are quite current. What are they for ?

They keep user preferences and login and password change info.

> The reason i ask is that i'm planning to do a fresh install version of 4.0E
> on this existing system (instead of installupdate) and after that i'll copy
> back the user related system files like /etc/passwd /etc/group

If you do installupdate, all these files should be preserved or converted to new
format. If you do a fresh install, you need to re-create all user accounts. One
way to do it is to add them with dxaccounts. Transfering user files will be a
manual job then (tar xf ... ; chown -R ...)

The other thing to do is to copy all those files, /etc/passwd, /etc/groups,
/tcb/files/auth/* and do the "convauth".

> Now for consistency, do i have to copy back the files from /tcb/files/auth
> after the installation or they don't matter.

Or you could just copy /etc/passwd and /etc/group and do "secsetup". That'll
convert it.

Good luck.

