Ellefson wrote:
> 
> Wondering how to deny host acces on DUNIX 4.0D or E.

There are three levels at which you can go on denying access.

1. IP
-----

Digital UNIX 4.0 has IP filtering mechanism. The file is /etc/ifaccess.conf and
the command is "ifconfig <INT> filter".

2. TCP
------

There are TCP Wrappers on IASS CD so you can implement access/deny based on IP
address and TCP port.

3. Application
--------------

If the application has mechanisms for controlling access, then that's it. Telnet
doesn't.

