Essential System Administration from the O'Reilly and Associates series
has gotten me out of a jam or two (even though my book is the older
version which refers to DUNIX as OSF). It covers many flavors of UNIX
including DUNIX (and AIX). In this case, it could be very helpful since
it shows how to perform common tasks on the many different flavors of
UNIX. It usually retails at most self-respecting book stores for around
$40-$60 (self-respecting as in any book store that carries the O'Reilly
series in their computer section).

If you'd prefer more specific (read dry), there's always the System
Management section of the DUNIX documentation. They are in HTML format
on the doc CD, or at:

http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/pub_page/doc_list.html

