Hi,

I had to deal with this on New Year's Eve.
Maybe I did something wrong with my DU4.0D but: using "alias" argument
didn't work. Modification of rc.config didn't work. Usually the whole
system hanged or it just didn't work.

After some research the only thing that worked for me was creating
/etc/rc3.d/S99_of_mine containing:

/sbin/ifconfig tu0 aliaslist a.b.c.d/e

(note that I had to use "aliaslist", not "alias" ; a.b.c.d is a new IP
address of I/F tu0, e - bitmask)


It would be interesting to know what's "the right solution". Anyway,
this works.

