I found the solution in http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/
Search the archives there. The method is to specify "rzxx" in disklabel.
Then it reads the Disk's parameters from the ST34371. Should work with
any modern SCSI Disk. I succeeded with a AtlasII 9GB equally.
> PS.
> Can you give me same instruction how to install that drive to my OSF/1 v3.2
> system.
Well, jumper a unique SCSI address, create appropriate partitions, and
newfs them. Then update /etc/fstab to get it mounted at reboot.
