Failed in what way?

Printer type:	remote
Remote machine:	122.111.222.1
Remote printer:	TEXT

And you get an ASCII network printer.

> I believe i need to do something to the /etc/printcap.
> by the way, i do not have any printer driver for the HP 4Si MX.
> this may be another problem ...... :(

Yes, you can (but don't have to) edit /etc/printcap, see man for
details. LPRsetup is easier.

As to the printer drivers, you actually have FILTERS, programs that will
convert ASCII stream into the HP LJ language. Maybe it can do the same
with PS stream. And your printer might be able to accept PS formatted
requests, so you dont have to bother with all this. Just find the right
queue name on your printer/JetDirect card.

Nix.
